<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Dominion of New England</h1><p class="st-meta">1686 CE – 1689 CE · capital Boston</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">James II's attempt to merge the colonies from Maine to New Jersey into one royal government without assemblies, overthrown by a Boston revolt in 1689.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the charter of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massachusetts-bay-colony">Massachusetts Bay Colony</a> was revoked in 1684, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James II</a> decided to combine the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> colonies under direct royal rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-dudley">Joseph Dudley</a> headed an interim government from 1686, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Sir Edmund Andros</a> arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> as governor in December 1686. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-new-york">Province of New York</a> and East and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-jersey">West Jersey</a> were added in 1688.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andros">Andros</a> ruled with an appointed council and no elected assembly, levied taxes without consent, restricted town meetings and questioned land titles granted under the old charters. He enforced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/navigation-acts">Navigation Acts</a> and held Anglican services in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> meeting house, angering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a>. Protests such as that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ipswich-massachusetts">Ipswich</a> minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-wise">John Wise</a> were punished. Andros governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> through his lieutenant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-nicholson">Francis Nicholson</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>News of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>, and on 18 April 1689 a crowd rose, jailing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andros">Andros</a>. The colonies restored their old governments, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-massachusetts-bay">Massachusetts</a> gained a new charter in 1691 as the Province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massachusetts-bay-colony">Massachusetts Bay</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dominion-of-new-england.jpg" alt="Dominion of New England" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_England_under_Sir_Edmund_Andros.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1686 CE – 1689 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Boston</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Joseph Dudley, Edmund Andros</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Puritanism, Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dominion of New England in America</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1688&amp;focus=dominion-of-new-england" aria-label="Dominion of New England on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2957 671 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dominion of New England lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3277 927L3282 940M3277 927L3283 922M3277 927L4970 663M3277 927L3293 904M3277 927L3258 951M3277 927L3231 946M3277 927L3186 980M3277 927L3177 986M3277 927L3174 997"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3282 940h0M3283 922h0M4970 663h0M3293 904h0M3258 951h0M3231 946h0M3186 980h0M3177 986h0M3174 997h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3277 927h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3277 927h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>